<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: A Sunny Day
</h4>

<p>
Hey, <br />
<br />
I work Saturday cops and was slated to write a story about the Flapjack Festival for Monday's paper. I covered it last year and wrote a pretty traditional "yum-yum-love-me-some-flapjacks" story  and I wanted to do something different this year, but wasn't sure what. I thought maybe I'd go there at night to check it out or to be there when the masses of volunteers closed it down on Sunday. <br />
I stopped in the office Saturday after checking the arrest reports to write some briefs and then head to an afternoon interview. I  talked with the photographer, Zach, who had been at the parade. He told me about Noodwang -- so all the kudos go to Zach. He is amazing. <br />
I called the PIO and asked for a jail interview with Noodwang. I'm so thankful for the PIO (as it was the weekend and he didn't even have to answer my call, let alone get this sorted for me.) I heard on Sunday that it was approved and went over and hung out with Noodwang for awhile. I'm so happy it all worked out!  <br />
<br />
Thanks, Sully, for what you said. I really appreciate it. <br />
<br />
Erin :) <br />
<br />
<br />

</p>
